bibliograph (0.5.25) unstable; urgency=high

  * Fix: the "For You" recommendations feed returned empty for every viewer
    since 0.5.23. `@atcute/client`'s `client.get` answers with a
    `{ ok, status, headers, data }` envelope, and `readViewerLibrary` read that
    envelope as the XRPC body; the shape guard rejected every page and the
    function returned null for every viewer, so every recommendation path
    returned `[]`. Unwrapped in both the library reader and the linklonk
    signal reader, matching the shelf/profile call sites.
  * "For You" now also ranks by a LinkLonk-style collaborative-filtering walk
    over the local Bookhive mirror (~144k records, 99% mapped to catalog
    editions), merged behind the viewer's subject-overlap candidates. Biblio
    shelving `read`/`reading` counts as an up and `dnf` as a down, and review
    ratings fold in the same way (>= 6 up, <= 5 down; a review without a
    rating counts as up). Down votes outrank ups on conflict. The graph is
    TTL-cached for 10 minutes and the viewer's own editions are never
    candidates.
  * Discover and Extended Network feeds no longer surface the signed-in
    viewer's own records: `paginateFromDb` drops them from the public feed and
    the extended feed removes the viewer from its 1-hop author set, so a
    self-follow cannot leak either. `following` keeps its raw set and
    anonymous callers see the unfiltered Discover feed.

