bibliograph (0.5.24) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Viewer-facing feeds served over XRPC now drop authors the viewer blocks —
    and authors who block the viewer — using marco.jazco.dev's public
    follow/block graph (`Relationships`, one call per page over at most 100
    candidates). Applies to the `following`, `extended` and `dynamic` feeds
    and to the network fallback page, for authenticated viewers only;
    anonymous callers are unchanged. `lib/server/marco.ts` treats an account
    as blocked only when its `block` entry carries `outUri`/`inUri`, since
    marco names every follow and block even where no record exists.
  * "For You" recommendations gain a third candidate source: editions the
    viewer's network mutuals shelved or reviewed, ranked by distinct mutual
    count against the local shelving/review mirror. The mutual list is
    marco's `Intersect` of follow OUT∩IN (5-minute cache, 256-DID cap) and
    merges in after active reads and past reads, so a reader with an empty
    shelf now gets an answer instead of nothing.
  * `MARCO_URL` selects the instance (default `https://marco.jazco.dev`; an
    explicitly empty value disables marco entirely) and `MARCO_TIMEOUT_MS`
    sets the per-call timeout (default 800 ms). Caveat: the public instance
    sees (viewer DID, candidate DID) pairs. Every marco failure logs and
    degrades to no annotation — unfiltered feeds, unsupplemented
    recommendations — and never errors a request.

