bibliograph (0.5.23) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Any XRPC read that serves books or contributors now heals what it returns.
    `lib/server/jobs/on-read.ts` adds `maybeEnqueueEditionBackfills` and
    `maybeEnqueueContributorBackfills`: one indexed `ANY()` query per batch
    selects only rows missing a field that has never been checked, and each
    missing description, cover, portrait or bio is enqueued fire-and-forget
    through the existing `jobKey`'d helpers, so a hot row cannot stack
    duplicates. Neither helper throws — a backfill that cannot be queued never
    fails the read that triggered it — and in steady state (nothing missing) a
    pass costs one query and enqueues nothing. Wired into `hydrateBooksByUri`,
    `searchEditions`, `resolveEditions`, `searchWorks` (contributors only),
    `searchContributors`, `getImageForBook` / `getImageForContributor` (which
    also gain the `cover_checked_at` gate) and `getEditionsByContributor`.
  * Contributor pages gain an administrators-only "Queue portrait + bio
    backfill" button, whose `runBackfill` action re-checks `isAdministrator`
    regardless of UI visibility and enqueues both contributor jobs. Enqueue-
    only: the action returns immediately and `bibliograph-worker.service`
    scrapes.
  * `backfill-contributor-bio` is now a real graphile task in
    `searchTaskList`. `backfillBioForContributor` previously had no
    registration point, so the module was dead code; it is reachable through
    the new `enqueueContributorBioBackfill` (`jobKey` `backfill-bio:<uri>`,
    maxAttempts 5) as well as the on-read helper and the contributor button.
    No migration: job names are not schema.

