bibliograph (0.5.19) unstable; urgency=medium

  * `getEditionsByContributor` now filters with jsonb containment
    (`contributors @> '[{"subject":{"uri":…}}]'`) instead of an `EXISTS` over
    `jsonb_array_elements`, which no index can serve. Every call that did not find
    `limit` rows near the top of `editions_created_at_idx` walked the whole 888MB
    catalog table: measured on lescayes at 11.7s for a contributor with 1008
    editions, with ten concurrent 34s calls all waiting on DataFileRead.
  * New `editions_contributors_gin` (GIN, jsonb_path_ops) serves the containment
    form, the same operator class `editions_identifiers_gin` already uses.
  * Results are unchanged: containment matched the EXISTS filter exactly on the
    sampled contributors (24222 and 1008 rows) because each stored element carries
    `role` and `subject{cid,uri}`, and containment ignores the extra keys.
  * No other behaviour change; migration 0031 applies on first start.

